{"error":false,"activeTest":false,"task":{"id":14253130,"type":"Review","status":"Processed","importance":1,"reason":null,"locked":null,"proofId":null,"currentQuestionId":null,"currentQuestionTimestamp":null,"progress":1,"points":7,"passed":1,"rawPointsAwarded":9,"pointsAwarded":9,"mp":null,"mpAwarded":null,"mpDecayRate":null,"student":{"id":57975,"firstName":"Harrison","lastName":"Charles","locale":null,"subscriptionId":"sub_1UO3yHD4gcTFRx97dYjQXmX1","sequenceId":19},"course":{"id":111,"name":"Mathematical Foundations II"},"topic":{"id":427,"name":"Dividing Polynomials Using Long Division"},"test":{"id":null,"name":null,"diagnostic":null,"timeLimit":null,"questionCount":null},"created":"2026-10-16T02:30:39.000Z","started":"2026-10-16T03:48:33.000Z","completed":"2026-10-16T03:49:42.000Z","processed":"2026-10-16T03:49:52.000Z","progressStr":"100%","answers":[{"id":62318113,"created":"2026-10-16T03:48:50.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":17746,"number":1,"createdStr":"Fri, Oct 16th @ 3:48 AM","timeElapsedFormatted":"0:18","question":{"id":18450,"format":"MC","difficulty":3,"exampleId":5144,"text":"<p>$\\dfrac{x^4+x^3+10x-5}{x^2-x+3}=$</p>\n","choice1":"$x^2+2x-1 + \\dfrac{3x-2}{x^2-x+3}$","choice2":"$x^2+2x-1 - \\dfrac{3x-2}{x^2-x+3}$","choice3":"$x^2+2x-1 +\\dfrac{x^2-x+3}{3x-2}$","choice4":"$x^2-2x-1 +\\dfrac{x-2}{x^2-x+3}$","choice5":"$x^2+2x+1 - \\dfrac{x-2}{x^2-x+3}$","freeAnswerChoice":"","explanation":"<p>Notice that the dividend is missing the $x^2$ term. So, we first rewrite it by including the missing term with a coefficient of zero, as follows:</p>\n<p>\\[\nx^4+x^3+10x-5 = x^4+x^3+{\\color{red}0}x^2+10x-5\n\\]</p>\n<p>Now, using the method of polynomial division, we obtain the following:</p>\n<p>\\begin{align*}\n\\require{enclose}\n& \\phantom{x^2-x+3} \\:\\:\\:\\:\\: x^2 + 2x-1 \\\\\n& x^2-x+3 \\: \\enclose{longdiv}{\\:\\, x^4+\\phantom{0}x^3+0x^2+10x-5 \\:\\:} \\\\\n& \\phantom{x^2-x+3} \\:\\:\\:\\:\\: \\underline{x^4-\\phantom{0}x^3+3x^2} \\\\\n& \\phantom{x^2-x+3} \\:\\:\\:\\:\\:\\:\\: \\phantom{x^4+} 2x^3-3x^2+10x-5 \\\\\n& \\phantom{x^2-x+3} \\:\\:\\:\\:\\:\\:\\: \\phantom{x^4+} \\underline{2x^3-2x^2+\\phantom{0}\n6x} \\\\\n& \\phantom{x^2-x+3} \\:\\:\\:\\:\\: \\phantom{x^4+2x^3} -\\phantom{0}x^2+\\phantom{0}4x-5 \\\\\n& \\phantom{x^2-x+3} \\:\\:\\:\\:\\:\\: \\phantom{x^4+2x^3} \\underline{-\\,\\phantom{0}x^2+\\phantom{00}x-3} \\\\\n& \\phantom{x^2-x+3} \\:\\:\\:\\:\\:\\:\\: \\phantom{x^4+2x^3-0x^2+} \\phantom{0}3x-2 \\\\\n\\end{align*}</p>\n<p>Therefore, </p>\n<ul>\n<li><p>the quotient is $x^2 +2x - 1,$ and </p>\n</li>\n<li><p>the remainder is ${3x-2}.$</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Therefore,\n\\[\n\\dfrac{x^4+x^3+10x-5}{x^2-x+3}=x^2+2x-1 + \\dfrac{3x-2}{x^2-x+3}.\n\\]</p>\n","topic":{"id":427,"name":"Dividing Polynomials Using Long Division"},"example":{"id":5144,"title":"Dividing Polynomials When the Dividend Contains Zero Coefficients"},"group":{"id":86453,"calculator":"None"},"graphics":[],"selects":[{"id":null,"number":null,"answers":[]}],"inputAnswers":[],"body":null,"taskId":14253130,"answer":{"id":62318113,"cread":"2026-10-16T03:48:50.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":17746},"graphic":false,"difficultyClass":"difficultyHard","difficultySymbol":"H","rendered":true,"testMode":false}},{"id":62318123,"created":"2026-10-16T03:49:10.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":14337,"number":2,"createdStr":"Fri, Oct 16th @ 3:49 AM","timeElapsedFormatted":"0:14","question":{"id":18481,"format":"MC","difficulty":2,"exampleId":5144,"text":"<p>What is the quotient of $-2x^4+x^3-3x^2+1$ divided by $2x^2-x+5?$</p>\n","choice1":"$-x^2+1$","choice2":"$x^2-1$","choice3":"$x^2+1$","choice4":"$-x^2-1$","choice5":"$-x^2$","freeAnswerChoice":"","explanation":"<p><p>Notice that the dividend is missing the $x$ term. So, we first rewrite it by including the missing term with a coefficient of zero, as follows:</p></p>\n<p><p>\\[\n-2x^4+x^3-3x^2+1 = -2x^4+x^3-3x^2+{\\color{red}0}x+1\n\\]</p></p>\n<p><p>Now, using the method of polynomial division, we obtain the following:</p></p>\n<p><p>\\begin{align*}\n\\require{enclose}\n& \\phantom{2x^2-x+5} \\:\\:\\:\\: {\\color{blue}-x^2 + 1} \\\\\n& 2x^2-x+5 \\: \\enclose{longdiv}{\\:\\, -2x^4+x^3-3x^2+0x+1 \\:\\:} \\\\\n& \\phantom{2x^2-x+5} \\:\\:\\:\\: \\underline{-\\,2x^4+x^3-5x^2} \\\\\n& \\phantom{2x^2-x+5} \\:\\:\\:\\:\\: \\phantom{-\\,2x^4+x^3-} 2x^2+0x+1 \\\\\n& \\phantom{2x^2-x+5} \\:\\:\\:\\:\\: \\phantom{-\\,2x^4+x^3-} \\underline{2x^2-\\phantom{0}x+5} \\\\\n& \\phantom{2x^2-x+5} \\:\\:\\:\\:\\: \\phantom{-\\,2x^4+x^3-3x^2+} {\\phantom{0}x-4} \\\\\n\\end{align*}</p></p>\n<p><p>Therefore, </p></p>\n<ul>\n<li><p>the quotient is ${\\color{blue}-x^2 + 1},$ and </p>\n</li>\n<li><p>the remainder is ${x-4}.$</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n","topic":{"id":427,"name":"Dividing Polynomials Using Long Division"},"example":{"id":5144,"title":"Dividing Polynomials When the Dividend Contains Zero Coefficients"},"group":{"id":86449,"calculator":"None"},"graphics":[],"selects":[],"inputAnswers":[],"body":null,"taskId":14253130,"answer":{"id":62318123,"cread":"2026-10-16T03:49:10.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":14337},"graphic":false,"difficultyClass":"difficultyModerate","difficultySymbol":"M","rendered":true,"testMode":false}},{"id":62318144,"created":"2026-10-16T03:49:41.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":null,"freeResponse":"[\"3x^2-x+3\",\"-9x\"]","timeElapsed":24873,"number":3,"createdStr":"Fri, Oct 16th @ 3:49 AM","timeElapsedFormatted":"0:25","question":{"id":270153,"format":"FR","difficulty":3,"exampleId":8932,"text":"Express $\\dfrac{15x^4+x^3+x^2+x-12}{5x^2+2x-4}$ in the form $q(x) + \\dfrac{r(x)}{5x^2+2x-4},$ where $q(x)$ is the quotient and $r(x)$ is the remainder of the division.$\\phantom{\\dfrac{x^2}{x}}$","choice1":" ","choice2":" ","choice3":" 