dden; border-left:hidden\">    $5x^2+2x-4$    </td>\n\n<td width=30 style=\"text-align:center; font-size: 0.9em; border-bottom:hidden; vertical-align: top; position: relative;\">\n  <div style=\"text-align:center; font-size: 0.9em; position: absolute; top: -9.5px; left: 50%; transform: translateX(-50%); \">__</div>\n</td>\n\n<td width=110 style=\"text-align:center; font-size: 0.9em; border-bottom:hidden; border-left:hidden; vertical-align: top; position: relative;\">\n  <div style=\"text-align:center; font-size: 0.9em; position: absolute; top: -9.5px; left: 50%; transform: translateX(-50%); \"></div>\n</td>\n\n<td width=30 style=\"text-align:center; border-bottom:hidden; border-top:hidden; border-left:hidden; vertical-align: bottom; font-size: 0.9em; position: relative;\">\n  <div style=\"text-align:center; font-size: 0.9em; position: absolute; bottom: 0px; left: 50%; transform: translateX(-50%); \"\"></td>\n\n<td width=\"100\" height=\"10\" style=\"text-align:center; vertical-align: top; border:1px solid black; border-right:hidden; border-left:hidden; border-bottom:hidden\">$5x^2+2x-4$    </td>\n</tr>\n\n</table>\n\n","explanation":"<p>Using the method of polynomial division, we obtain the following:</p>\n<p>\\begin{align*}\n\\require{enclose}\n& \\phantom{5x^2+2x-4} \\:\\:\\:\\:\\: {3x^2-x+3} \\\\\n& {5x^2+2x-4} \\: \\enclose{longdiv}{\\:\\, 15x^4+\\phantom{0}x^3+\\phantom{00}x^2+\\phantom{0}x-12 \\:\\:} \\\\\n& \\phantom{5x^2-2x+4} \\:\\:\\:\\:\\: \\underline{15x^4+6x^3-12x^2} \\\\\n& \\phantom{5x^2-2x+4} \\:\\:\\:\\:\\: \\phantom{15x^4} -5x^3+13x^2+\\phantom{0}x-12 \\\\\n& \\phantom{5x^2-2x+4} \\:\\:\\:\\:\\:\\: \\phantom{15x^4} \\underline{- \\, 5x^3-\\phantom{0}2x^2+4x} \\\\\n& \\phantom{5x^2-2x+4} \\:\\:\\:\\:\\:\\: \\phantom{15x^4-5x^3} \\:\\:\\:\\: {15x^2-3x-12} \\\\\n& \\phantom{5x^2-2x+4} \\:\\:\\:\\:\\:\\: \\phantom{15x^4-5x^3} \\:\\:\\:\\: \\underline{15x^2+6x-12} \\\\\n& \\phantom{5x^2-2x+4} \\:\\:\\:\\:\\:\\: \\phantom{15x^4-5x^3+15x^2} {- \\, 9x}\n\\end{align*}</p>\n<p>As a result, </p>\n<ul>\n<li><p>the quotient is ${3x^2-x+3},$ and </p>\n</li>\n<li><p>the remainder is ${-9x}.$</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Therefore,</p>\n<p>\\begin{align*}\n\\dfrac{15x^4+x^3+x^2+x-12}{5x^2+2x-4} \n&= \\bbox[4pt,border: 1px solid lightgray]{3x^2-x+3} + \\dfrac{\\bbox[4pt,border: 1px solid lightgray]{(-9x)}}{5x^2+2x-4}.\n\\end{align*}</p>\n","topic":{"id":427,"name":"Dividing Polynomials Using Long Division"},"example":{"id":8932,"title":"Dividing a Quartic Polynomial by a Quadratic or Cubic Polynomial"},"group":{"id":86460,"calculator":"None"},"graphics":[],"selects":[],"inputAnswers":[],"body":null,"taskId":14253130,"answer":{"id":62318144,"cread":"2026-10-16T03:49:41.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":null,"freeResponse":["3x^2-x+3","-9x"],"timeElapsed":24873},"graphic":false,"freeResponse":{"segments":[{"text":"<table rules=all cellpadding=1 align=\"center\" style=\"border:1px solid black; margin: auto; margin-bottom: 10mm; margin-top: 4mm\">\n\n<td width=\"130\" height=\"10\" style=\"text-align:center; vertical-align: bottom; border:1px solid black; border-right:hidden; border-top:hidden; border-left:hidden\">$15x^4+x^3+x^2+x-12$</td>\n\n<td width=30 style=\"text-align:center; border-bottom:hidden; border-top:hidden; vertical-align: bottom; font-size: 0.9em; position: relative;\">\n  <div style=\"text-align:center; font-size: 0.9em; position: absolute; bottom: -1px; left: 50%; transform: translateX(-50%); \"\">__</td>\n\n<td width=110 style=\"text-align:center; border-bottom:hidden; border-top:hidden; border-left:hidden; vertical-align: bottom; position: relative;\">\n  <div style=\"text-align:center; position: absolute; bottom: -12px; left: 50%; transform: translateX(-50%); \"\">"},{"textbox":{"answer":"3x^2-x+3","type":"expression","width":100,"margin":{"left":0,"right":0},"buttons":["frac","exp"]}},{"text":"</td>\n\n<td width=30 style=\"text-align:center; border-bottom:hidden; border-top:hidden; border-left:hidd